<!-- file-explorer-pal.xhtpm - real, shared File Explorer widget.
     11.brainstorm/2026-09-05/PDL-READER-AND-FILE-EXPLORER-WIDGET.md.

     Static template + real manager (file_explorer_manager.+x, a
     <module>), same house convention every other widget this session
     touched already uses (taskbar-settings, swatch-picker, open-hai).
     The manager owns the actual directory scan/navigation/pick state
     and publishes it as file_explorer_ui.txt; this template only
     ever renders whatever it published, via vars=.

     REAL FIX 2026-09-05, found live testing this exact window twice:
     (1) vars= resolves a relative token against g_package_dir (this
     widget's OWN directory, since that's where this file lives) -
     just the bare filename is correct here, not a path repeating
     this widget's own directory a second time. (2) <scrolllist> is
     ONLY ever laid out by layout_sidebar_panel() (khtpm_core_render.c),
     which requires BOTH a <sidebar> AND a <panel> child of <page> -
     a bare top-level <scrolllist> with neither never gets sized at
     all (confirmed live: x/y stuck at a default, w/h stayed 0).
     Restructured to match bookmarks-pal.xhtpm's own real, working
     shape - <sidebar> holds the directory listing, <panel> holds the
     Save-As controls (LOAD mode's panel just shows the current path).

     FE_ENTRY:<n> / FE_SAVEAS / FE_CANCEL are real, generic dispatch
     verbs khtpm_core_render.c's own dispatch() handles in-process
     (same exact "write an incrementing-seq action file the manager
     polls" convention PICK:<n> already uses for taskbar-settings) -
     not a launched shell relay script, which would have no reliable
     way to know its own absolute install path from inside a static
     template. `${entry.type} ${entry.name} ${entry.size}` is a plain,
     honest label (no icons/formatting yet - real v1 scope, not a
     placeholder left unfinished).

     SAVE mode's filename field is a real, generic <cli_io> - typing
     into it is handled entirely by the shared renderer itself
     (default_cli_io_handle_key(), this session's own real cursor
     work). FE_SAVEAS reads this field's LIVE value directly off the
     tree (dispatch()'s own find_by_id("filename")) rather than a
     `${filename}` substitution, which would only ever reflect the
     manager's last-published value, not every keystroke.
     show="${show_save_row}" hides the whole row in LOAD mode (manager
     publishes show_save_row=0/1 based on its own mode=).

     REAL FIX 2026-09-05, direct live report ("chrome has 2 exit
     buttons as a bug? that shouldn't be possible") - it wasn't a
     rendering bug: EVERY sidebar+panel window already gets a real,
     free auto-generated chrome "X" (g_default_close_elem, injected
     outside this template entirely, top-right corner) - the explicit
     `<item id="cancel" class="close-btn">` below was a genuinely
     redundant SECOND close button this template added on top of it.
     Removed - dismissal is the free chrome X, same as every other
     sidebar+panel window in the house already relies on. -->

<window label="File Explorer - ${mode}" class="file-explorer-pal database-window user-resizable" vars="file_explorer_ui.txt">
  <!-- REAL, NEW 2026-09-05 - launch_module() passes house_root then
       package_dir automatically, then this <module>'s own id= as a
       THIRD, single extra argv slot (kh_collect_and_launch_modules()'s
       own real convention - id doubles as extra_arg when set, same as
       every other module-launching widget in the house). That extra
       slot carries the browse mode; the manager always starts
       browsing at house_root itself (a real, honest v1 default - see
       file_explorer_manager.c's own header for why a configurable
       start_dir isn't wired up yet).

       REAL FIX 2026-09-15, direct live reports ("its ugly and hard to
       use", "the other half is completely empty side pane, thats
       bad", "should show current file path as buttons... jump to
       that dir", "window should be resizable"):
       - `user-resizable` added - the same free, generic ⌟ drag-grip
         every other opted-in HQ window already gets, no new code.
       - The dead, mostly-empty `<panel>` in LOAD mode is real, not
         cosmetic - `layout_sidebar_panel()`'s own gate (confirmed
         this same session, DSR's own toy) requires BOTH a real
         `<sidebar>` and a real `<panel>` or the whole window falls to
         a tiny no-chrome fallback, so it can't just be deleted. Given
         real width instead (`.fe-panel` in the CSS) so it reads as a
         real, if secondary, region (SAVE mode's own filename+Save
         controls) rather than a wasted half-window - and `.sidebar`
         widened to do the real majority of the work, matching what
         the user is actually looking at 95% of the time.
       - `${dir}`'s own plain, unclickable label replaced with a real
         breadcrumb - one button per real ancestor path segment
         (file_explorer_manager.c's own new build_crumbs()/CRUMB:<n>),
         each jumps straight to that directory. -->
  <module src="&.widgits/file-explorer/ops/+x/file_explorer_manager.+x" id="LOAD"/>
  <page name="main">
    <sidebar id="sidebar" class="sidebar">
      <repeat count="${n_crumbs}" bind="crumb">
      <item id="crumb${crumb.#}" class="fe-crumb" action="FE_CRUMB:${crumb.#}" label="${crumb.label}"/>
      </repeat>
      <scrolllist>
        <repeat count="${n_entries}" bind="entry">
        <item id="entry${entry.#}" class="fe-entry" action="FE_ENTRY:${entry.#}" label="${entry.icon}  ${entry.name} ${entry.size}"/>
        </repeat>
      </scrolllist>
    </sidebar>
    <panel id="panel" class="fe-panel">
      <text label="Pick a file to load." class="quiet" show="${show_load_hint}"/>
      <cli_io id="filename" target_id="filename" label="Save as: " show="${show_save_row}"/>
      <item id="save" class="opacity-btn" show="${show_save_row}" action="FE_SAVEAS" label="Save"/>
    </panel>
  </page>
</window>
